        "author": "Vineeth B",
        "rating": 1,
        "date": "7 months ago",
        "comment": "Extremely Poor Experience – Not Worth the Money\n\nI conducted my wedding at Safina Plaza on 21st January and had a very disappointing and stressful experience due to extremely poor management.\n\nThe event was scheduled for 3:00 PM, but even at 3:30 PM the staff were still cleaning the hall. Chairs were not arranged, the sound system was not ready, and there was no coordination at all. Because of this, the wedding finally started only at 4:30 PM, delaying everything.\n\nI paid a total of ₹1,05,750 including ₹35k for indoor decoration, but the decoration quality was very poor. Around 80% of the flowers were artificial, which was never informed in advance. The stage background was completely different from what was shown during booking, and the stage steps were not fixed properly, even after repeatedly asking the team to correct it.\n\nThere was zero time management. Nothing was done at the promised time, and we had to constantly follow up for every basic arrangement, even after full payment. My point of contact was Danish, and the head in charge was Rony, but there was no accountability or proper supervision. The team was inexperienced, and issues were not handled professionally.\n\nRoom allocation was also very inconvenient. Despite having three floors, two rooms were provided—one on a different floor and another one was 1km away , where they informed me that was on the next building from the banquet hall. There were multiple events happening at the same time, but no proper signboards or staff guidance for guests. Washrooms were available only on the first floor, which caused inconvenience.\n\nOverall, I am completely dissatisfied with their service. Instead of enjoying my wedding day,\nI was stressed throughout due to their mismanagement.\nI would never recommend Safina banquet to anyone\nI couldn’t even give 1star Rating",
