        "comment": "Worst Experience Ever - Avoid This Venue at All Costs!.\n\nWe had the misfortune of booking Huq House for our event, and it was an unmitigated disaster. The management's incompetence and lack of concern for customer satisfaction are appalling.\n\nFrom the outset, we requested that the front glass door be cleaned, which they claimed had already been done. However, when I showed them the dirty door, they reluctantly agreed to send someone to clean it. After 20 minutes, the cleaning staff arrived, but they used dirty cloths and left soap water stains on the door. We brought this to their attention again, and they shrugged it off, saying, \"That's all we can do.\"\n\nThe Hub Hall's decoration team, led by Arun, was equally unprofessional. They delayed setting up the decorations, and when we asked Arun about the incomplete work, he dismissively said, \"Whatever is there, that's all. If you want anything, go to the office and talk to management.\"\n\nWe visited the office to request that two mats be placed under the stage due to broken tiles. The management agreed, but after an hour, nothing had been done. When we followed up, they refused to fulfill our request, responding with rude behavior.\n\nTo add insult to injury, we booked decorations through the Hub Hall itself, but Arun, the decoration team member, had the audacity to restrict our music choices, saying no DJ remixes were allowed. It's outrageous that we paid for services that were not delivered.\n\nFurthermore, the restrooms were in a deplorable state. They were not cleaned or maintained properly, with overflowing trash cans, dirty sinks, and toilets that were not fit for use. This was not only unpleasant but also a serious health concern.\n\nAdditionally, the air conditioning system was not functioning properly, leaving our guests sweating and uncomfortable. Despite our requests to adjust the temperature, the staff seemed incapable of resolving the issue.\n\nTo make matters worse, the venue provided no proper support or parking facilities. They instructed our guests to park their cars and bikes on the roadside, forcing them to walk an unacceptable distance of 400-500 meters to reach the venue. This was not only inconvenient but also a safety concern.\n\nOther issues we faced included:\n\n- Poor communication and unresponsive staff\n- Lack of attention to detail and cleanliness\n- Unprofessional behavior from management and staff\n- Misrepresentation of services and amenities\n- Overcharging for subpar services\n\nDo not, I repeat, DO NOT book this venue for any event. The pictures they show are deceiving, and the reality is a nightmare. We demand a full refund and compensation for the stress and disappointment caused.\n\nRating: -5/0 stars (if that were possible)\n\nAvoid Huq House at all costs. Your event deserves better.",
        "avatarUrl": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIO7I7ryWaTEsBR4I76bG5Kp5P2-gQE0cXPXGUy5cBjYwJ3aQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
